### 1. Insert identical data into both tables (replaces previous experiment data)
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"mutation { seedUsers(rowCount: 100000) { rowsPerTable } }"}

### 2. Search without an email index
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{ search(table: TABLE1, email: \"user50000@example.com\") { table elapsedMs users { id name email age } } }"}

### 3. Search with an email index
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{ search(table: TABLE2, email: \"user50000@example.com\") { table elapsedMs users { id name email age } } }"}

### 4. Compare repeated measurements and actual plans
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{ benchmark(email: \"user50000@example.com\", repetitions: 20, warmup: 3) { email warmup repetitions speedup table1 { table matchedRows averageMs medianMs minMs maxMs samplesMs explainAnalyze } table2 { table matchedRows averageMs medianMs minMs maxMs samplesMs explainAnalyze } } }"}

### 5. A nonexistent email: both queries return no users
POST http://localhost:8080/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{ benchmark(email: \"missing@example.com\") { speedup table1 { matchedRows medianMs explainAnalyze } table2 { matchedRows medianMs explainAnalyze } } }"}
